'''''Test Tower''''' is a South Korean [[webtoon]] written and illustrated by a
creator. It has been serialised since 2010 and the infobox above is article
furniture that no summary should ever contain.

== Synopsis ==
A boy who has spent his whole life beneath the tower follows the one person he
cares about through its door, and finds a place that measures everyone who
enters it. Each floor sets a test, and each test asks for something different:
strength on one, trust on another, and on the worst of them a willingness to
spend other people to get higher.<ref name="review">A citation that must not
appear in the summary.</ref>

He climbs anyway, because the person he followed is somewhere above him, and
the tower has never once been generous about telling him how far.

=== Premise ===
The tower grants whoever reaches its top whatever they want, which is the
promise that keeps the floors full of people willing to be measured. Nobody
who has reached the top has come back down to say whether the promise is kept.

=== Characters ===
* A boy, the protagonist, whose name is a character-list entry and not narrative.
* A guide, who administers the tests on the lower floors.

